Third-party assets bundled with this application
================================================

Default hit samples
-------------------

`public/samples/Gameplay/` contains audio sample files taken verbatim from

    ppy/osu-resources  --  https://github.com/ppy/osu-resources

specifically its `osu.Game.Resources/Samples/Gameplay/` tree, retaining that
tree's three-tier layout (`ArgonPro/`, `Argon/`, and the shared tier beside
them) so they resolve the way osu!lazer's own skins resolve them.

Those files are licensed under

    Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
    (CC BY-NC 4.0)  --  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

Copyright (c) ppy Pty Ltd <contact@ppy.sh>.

The licence requires attribution -- this notice -- and bars commercial use of
anything these files ship inside. This application is a personal,
non-commercial tool.

Only `.wav` and `.mp3` sample files are taken. The osu-resources fonts are
separately licensed and are not included, and the osu! and ppy trademarks are
excluded from the CC grant and are not used.

The osu!std-relevant subset is vendored: per-bank hit samples
(`{bank}-hit{normal,whistle,finish,clap}`), slider samples
(`{bank}-slider{tick,slide,whistle}`), the spinner samples and `combobreak`.
Files belonging to the other rulesets (`taiko-*`, `catch-banana`) and to game
surfaces this application does not have (`failsound*`, `rank-*`, `fountain-*`,
`nightcore-*`, `restart`, `resume-countdown`, `pause-loop`, `sectionfail`,
`sectionpass`) are not included.

Classic default skin assets
---------------------------

`public/skins/legacy/` contains image files taken verbatim from the same
repository, specifically its `osu.Game.Resources/Skins/Legacy/` tree at

    tag 2026.710.0  --  commit d8d01c29ce0f298159aea3644b947d8b4a1882a2

which is the exact `ppy.osu.Game.Resources` version the pinned osu!lazer
checkout references, so this art is what that lazer would itself draw.

They ship under the same CC BY-NC 4.0 grant and for the same reason: osu!lazer
never renders a legacy skin against lazer art, so a legacy skin missing an
element needs somewhere of its OWN era to fall through to. Almost every real
skin is incomplete -- most ship no follow point, no spinner background, no
slider score point -- so without this set the normal case would be a playfield
half legacy and half Argon, a look that has never existed in any osu! client.

The osu!std gameplay subset is vendored: the cursor set, the hit circle and
its overlay, the approach circle, the combo number glyphs, the slider ball
frames, the follow circle, the slider score point, the reverse arrow, the
follow point, the four judgement grades, hit lighting, and the spinner. Files
belonging to the other rulesets (`taiko-*`, `mania-*`, `fruit-*`,
`pippidon*`), to game surfaces this application does not have (menu, ranking,
results, scorebar, the score and combo fonts, the input overlay), to the
editor (`hitcircleselect`), and to judgements this ruleset does not draw per
object (`hit300g`, `hit100k`, `hit300k`) are not included.

Everything else in this repository is the project's own work; osu!lazer is
referenced for behavioural parity only, and no lazer source code is included.
